# 1. Users & JWT: registration, login, two roles (Customer, Admin).
#
# VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each request.
# Send TOP TO BOTTOM the first time: later requests reuse the responses of earlier ones,
# e.g. "loginA.response.body.$.accessToken" is the token from the request named loginA.
# This file logs in 2 times (login is limited to 5 per minute; on 429 wait a minute).
# The admin login is read from api-tests/.env (ADMIN_EMAIL, ADMIN_PASSWORD), which git ignores.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@adminEmail = {{$dotenv ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@adminPassword = {{$dotenv ADMIN_PASSWORD}}


### Register customer A → 201 (role: Customer, Location header)
# @name registerA
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer.a.{{$timestamp}}@shop.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Register customer B, trying to make itself Admin → 201, still "role": "Customer"
# Mass assignment: the extra "role" field is ignored, so nobody can register as an admin.
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer.b.{{$timestamp}}@shop.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### Register with an email that already exists → 409 Conflict
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{registerA.response.body.$.email}}",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Register with invalid input → 422, each field listed under "errors"
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### Login customer A → 200 + JWT
# @name loginA
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{registerA.response.body.$.email}}",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Login admin → 200 + JWT with "role": "Admin"
# The admin is created at startup from .env. No API can create an admin.
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### Who am I (customer A) → 200
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Who am I without a token → 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Garbage token → 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer this.is.not-a-real-token

### List users as customer → 403 (admin only)
GET {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### List users as admin → 200
GET {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get one user as admin → 200
GET {{api}}/users/{{registerA.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
